  "reason": "Evidence: The largest performance jump so far came from moving singleprofile→multiprofile (config_002: 0.535 → config_021: 0.629), and the current best (config_021) uses avgpool aggregation. We have no multiprofile data with transformer aggregation, leaving open whether a more expressive aggregation could further improve over simple averaging. Question: config_038 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) is identical to config_021 except aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer, cleanly isolating the effect of aggregation strategy. Why best next experiment: It is a single-variable ablation on the most promising configuration, directly testing whether the multiprofile gain can be amplified by learned aggregation. If transformer aggregation helps, it opens a rich sub-space (configs 045, 035, 036, etc.); if it does not, it confirms avgpool is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or image encoder variations in the multiprofile setting. This is more informative than testing fusion (concat≈weighted already shown in singleprofile) or switching encoders (higher risk of confounding)."
}

